title Four ceilings answered in one word, and each got its own line
prompt The autonomous fleet baton and construction/ITINERARY.md -- take the next agent-doable lap in the Glow language lane, reds first
think Reds first, and both of mine were one command. The cold endurance run named built_tool_freshness stale_tool with rye/bin/rye 30,638 seconds behind rye/src/main.rye, and ryekey red beside it reading another spelling of one toolchain changed the key. sh rye/bootstrap.sh closed both, which is the third firing of the cure copal published this morning.
think The keystone was my own last lap's named next fall. glow/tokens.rye returned error.BadToken from four different ceiling comparisons, so a caller met one word for a name too long, a cord interior too long, a hex literal with too many digits, and a source too long.
think The shape is rune_shape.parse_source_reporting's, one module over: thread a refusal.Slot pointer through the private lexers, seat tokenize_reporting beside tokenize, and let the published entry delegate through a scratch slot so its bytes and its signature both stand. The rota's dual seat names that move -- diverge by strengthening, never by rewriting.
think The four name a token KIND rather than a face, and that is the one design call. rune_shape names the face that would not fit; a lexer cannot, because the text that overran is exactly the text that will not fit inside max_field_name_bytes. So ident, tag, cord, hex, source -- and scan_ident_span takes its kind word from the caller, since the %tag path and the ident path share one scanner.
think The hex ceiling counts digits rather than bytes. Two digits make one byte, so a shared byte unit would report half the number max_hex_lit_digits is written in.
obs The mutations were run rather than reasoned. Swapping the hex unit to byte, replacing the tag kind word with ident, and dropping the source record each reddened the witness, so all three legs are load-bearing rather than decorative.
obs My QA frame closed on a measurement. glow/refusal.rye grades C+/76 and register is why -- 6 of its 8 counted head sentences are counted by the one word refusal, which is the module's name, its type's name and its subject. Struck tree-wide in a pen the file falls 23 negatives to 12 and still reads 35 percent, so a remainder is real; yet 4 of those 12 are counted on a declaration line, where pub const Slot = ?Refusal scores negative because a type is named Refusal.
obs I stopped the cold endurance run at 213 guards of 310 rather than hold the lap another hour. Six ships shared the pier and it had spent 43 minutes; fleet_call.sh --signal TERM reached exactly my pid and refused three peer trees out loud by name.
rota lap 5102, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; advanced by hand past row 2, which this tree read at 09:06. Its dual seat, How We Grow a Language, names this lap's move exactly: diverge by strengthening rather than rewriting, additive and behavior-preserving, nothing taken away once given.
